From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: mnt-sc: strip vendor prefix in spi_device_id table

mntsc_spi_dev_id[] carries the full "mntre,system-controller" compatible
string as its id name. The SPI core strips the vendor prefix off the DT
compatible string before matching against a driver's id_table (see the
"Strip off any vendor prefix" block in __spi_register_driver(),
drivers/spi/spi.c), so it looks up "system-controller", not
"mntre,system-controller". With the prefix left in, the id never matches,
and per that same function's comment, SPI module autoloading depends on
this id_table match, not on the of_match_table compatible string: "For
Really Good Reasons we use spi: modaliases not of: modaliases for DT so
module autoloading won't work if we don't have a spi_device_id as well as
a compatible string."

Practical effect: mnt_sc.ko is never auto-loaded by udev at boot, even
when the DTB correctly declares a "mntre,system-controller" node and the
module is present under /lib/modules. Confirmed on RK3588S (Radxa CM5):
`modprobe mnt_sc` binds and probes fine (driver reports "MNT System
Controller v4"), but nothing triggers that modprobe automatically.

reform2_lpc.c, the sibling driver this one was adapted from, already
strips the prefix correctly (g_spi_dev_id_list[] uses "lpc11u24", not
"mntre,lpc11u24"), so this is a straightforward port oversight, not a
deliberate choice - no comment in this driver, the patch that added it,
or elsewhere in the kernel tree explains keeping the prefix, and no other
driver in the tree registers "system-controller" as a spi_device_id name,
so there's no collision risk motivating it either.

Fix: drop the vendor prefix, matching reform2_lpc.c's convention.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/firmware/mnt-sc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/mnt-sc.c b/drivers/firmware/mnt-sc.c
index 8bcda2173b3b..1a2b3c4d5e6f 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/mnt-sc.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/mnt-sc.c
@@ -728,7 +728,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id of_mntre_sc_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, of_mntre_sc_match);

 static struct spi_device_id mntsc_spi_dev_id[] = {
-	{ "mntre,system-controller", 0 },
+	{ "system-controller", 0 },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(spi, mntsc_spi_dev_id);
